## Voltage - nano interface colors.
## Colors are xterm-256 palette indices, each the closest slot to the Voltage hex
## value in docs/palette.md. install.sh rewrites them to named colors on nano < 6.0.
## For the best match, set your terminal background to #0d1117.
## These `set` lines are inlined into ~/.nanorc by install.sh (nano does not allow
## `set` inside included files); the syntax/ files are included as-is.

set titlecolor bold,45,233
set statuscolor bold,233,45
set errorcolor bold,233,205
set selectedcolor 231,24
set numbercolor 243
set scrollercolor 243
set keycolor bold,45,232
set functioncolor 251,232
set promptcolor 231,233
set spotlightcolor 233,220
